        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दिक़्क़त",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिक़्क़त — diqqat — \"a difficulty, a hassle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अगर कोई दिक़्क़त होगी तो मुझे फ़ोन करो। agar koī diqqat hogī to mujhe fon karo. If there's any difficulty, phone me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिक़्क़त (diqqat) is usually traced to Arabic diqqa, \"fineness, exactness\", which reached Hindi through Persian. The sense of a difficulty is a Persian and Hindi one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
